<h2>What a plugin is</h2>

<p>An ES module that default-exports an object. The viewer imports it before it parses the slides:</p>

<code lang=js>
  export default {
    name: 'demo',
    tags: { badge: { doc: 'A label.', render: ({ attrs, text }) => `<b>${text}</b>` } },
    themes: { sepia: { '--bg': '#f4ecd8' } },
    tools: [{ title: 'Hi', icon: '<svg …/>', run: (api) => api.player.next() }],
    hooks: { step: (api, { slide }) => console.log(slide) },
  }
</code>

<p>Plugins are listed in <c>deck.json</c>: <c>"plugins": ["./demo.js", "@someone/slideit-plugin-qr"]</c>.</p>

<badge color=blue>docs/plugins.md</badge>
